# Zone 1, room 12: Kindle-dash (BUILD.md s5 tech 12, "universal with the Kindle Votive: dash through a
# wax wall ... to ignite it. Taught by a wax door"; docs/adr/0010 "Kindle-dash"). Grey box, not art.
#
# The game boots with the Kindle Votive (game/main.gd); fixtures say "option kindle 1".
#
# The route, west door to east door, 60 x 34 tiles (the camera's 1080 p view is 33.75 tiles):
#  1. A flat run, then a SAFE first wax: a screen one tile thick (x 704..736), floor to ceiling, in
#     the open with nothing to fall into. Dash into it: it ignites and the dash goes on through it.
#  2. A real use: a spike chasm 192 u wide (x 1088..1280, spikes 160 u below the floor) whose far lip
#     is capped by a WAX DOOR two tiles thick (x 1280..1344), floor to ceiling. A jump clears the
#     chasm, but the door stands where the landing would be: dash into it from the air, burn through
#     (the air jump comes back as the dash passes the wax) and land on the far ledge.
#  3. 512 u of floor to the east door.
#
# Why Kindle is the only way across: the wax is a wall like any other without the Votive
# (tech12_wax_blocks_without_kindle) and both screens run from the floor to the ceiling, so nothing
# goes over or under them; a jump cannot clear a wall 512 u tall, and the pit below the door has
# spikes, nothing to stand on. Controls: zone1/12_no_kindle_screen_holds,
# zone1/12_no_kindle_door_holds.
#
# Stand-ins: the wax is a "tag=wax" solid and the pit is a row of spikes (a hazard is a respawn at
# the safe point: the last ground the player stood on). The Snuffed that BUILD.md names beside wax
# does not exist yet. A skilled run is about 4 s (74 u to the door at 9 u/f run, 180 u dashes).
#
# Doors: west and east are 128 u (4 tiles) tall, standing on the floor at y 544.
room zone1/12_kindle_dash
size 60 34
spawn 200 544
tiles
